onunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Writing a Product Review", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<br>A product review is a report that gives someone's opinion about the quality of a product. You can use the Simple Present tense when you write a product review.<br>  <br>To write a review, you must include:<br> <br><span class=\"strong\">Features</span>:  information on what the product does and details<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Target Group</span>: information on who uses the product and why they would want to use it<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Pros and Cons</span>: an opinion about the positives and negatives of the product<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Overall Opinion</span>: your opinion of the product<br><br/><span class = \"italic\">Example</span>: <br/>Do you like to cook?<br/>(<span class = \"strong\">Target Group</span>)Our cookware is perfect for the busy parent! <br/>(<span class = \"strong\">Features</span>)It has stainless steel handles, so you won't burn yourself!<br/>(<span class = \"strong\">Pros/Cons</span>)It's large enough to cook an entire roast, but can get quite heavy!<br/>(<span class = \"strong\">Overall opinion</span>)I would say this product is overall a smart choice.", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consumer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who buys goods and services", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many consumers buy over the Internet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le09ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about shopping.", 